# Treat every file as binary — no line-ending translation, ever.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AND WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS:
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. CK3 mod files are text (.txt, .yml, .gui, .mod), so that rewrite
# changes their bytes — and CK3's multiplayer checksum is computed over the
# loaded files. A checksum that drifts by even one byte means you can't join a
# friend who is running the Workshop copy.
#
# `* -text` disables the conversion for everything, so what git hands back is
# byte-for-byte what went in.
* -text

# Belt and braces for the formats that are already binary.
*.dds  binary
*.mesh binary
*.anim binary
*.ogg  binary
*.wav  binary
*.png  binary
*.tga  binary
